  "notes": {
    "goals": "Goal ids are unique per family; `avoid` lists features the goal would leave unused (the level ends before they matter); `kind` names the objective kind when it differs (the rescue family's 'clear the pass' is clear_zones, defend's 'train N defenders' is hire). `adds` lists features the goal pulls in (shelves_full adds hunting, so the kiosk sells a hunted good beside the farmed one and every shelf takes planning); `needs` lists features the goal requires (@two_goods: at least two sellable goods). `anchor`: the goal puts a pad on the bot's plan that anchored features can hang their pads from.",
    "features": "`anchor` features add pads the bot only buys when they sit on its plan, so they need an anchoring goal. `with` pulls in companion features (salvage upgrades need turrets, tier 2 needs the material processor).",
    "composer": "The generator's add-on composer (generator src/composer.ts). A feature may join a level of its own family from `firstLevel` on, and a family's `guests` name other families' features it may borrow from that level on; a goal's `adds` count only once unlocked. `dStep` is the feature's measured difficulty step [lo, hi] (ops docs/reference/addons.md); a level's estimate is the family `base` plus the steps. `moduleCap` caps optional modules by target D ([upTo, cap] rows, first row whose upTo >= target); over the cap the newest extra goes. `extras` caps the features beyond the required ones (introduced, goal needs, finale) per phase (intro levels teach their new feature alone). `fixed` families keep the sequencer's set and never swap (defend D is a cliff, not a slope). After the knob search, at most `maxSwaps` add-on swaps (add one when every measured D is under the target, drop one when every one is over).",
    "finales": "Every 10th level combines two families: the first is the level's family and goal, the second adds its core modules and one feature. Rescue never pairs with defend (content: lasso excludes defense)."
